--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE

The MIT licence above covers the SOURCE CODE and the plugin built from it:
everything under src/, tools/, the build and packaging scripts, the PrismaUI
view (prisma-patch/), the FOMOD installer and the documentation.

It does NOT cover the licensed third-party assets in this repository:

  Sound effects (sounds/, shipped as Sound/fx/isekai/)
      UI Sound Pack by Nathan Gibson (Cyrex Studios), used under the Creative
      Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

      They may be redistributed and reused, commercially included, on one
      condition: Nathan Gibson is credited and this notice travels with them.
      That is a different licence from the MIT terms above, not a restriction
      on reuse - you may keep these files in a fork, you may not drop the
      credit.

  3D assets (meshes/, textures/)
      Generated with Meshy (https://www.meshy.ai) and used under the Creative
      Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

      Meshy's terms assign ownership of free-plan output to Meshy and license it
      back under CC BY 4.0. As with the sound effects, that permits redistribution
      and commercial use on one condition: Meshy is credited and this notice
      travels with the files. Keep them in a fork; do not drop the credit.

  Skill-tree node icons (icons/spells_*_frame.png, 40 files)
      From a purchased icon pack, credited in README.md. Its licence allows use
      in commercial and non-commercial projects and asks for no attribution,
      but it forbids redistributing the icons as part of another asset pack,
      and it is granted to the purchaser rather than to the work.

      So they are not relicensable under the MIT terms above, and forking this
      repository does not hand you the right to use them: replace them, or buy
      your own licence for the pack. This is a narrower permission than the
      sound effects above, which anyone may redistribute under CC BY 4.0.

The remaining 35 icons (blessings, ranks, shop, UI) are AI-generated artwork
made for this mod and ARE covered by the MIT licence above. That they are
AI-generated is not what decides it - the 3D assets above are AI-generated too
and are not covered. What decides it is the terms of the tool that produced
them.

THIRD-PARTY CODE

  CommonLibSSE-NG, Dear ImGui, spdlog and fmt are used under their own MIT
  licences. The PrismaUI API header (src/PrismaUI_API.h) is vendored from the
  PrismaUI SKSE example plugin, which invites exactly that use.

  extern/imgui-vr-helper/ is the client API of ImGuiVRHelper by alandtse,
  vendored verbatim and used under the LGPL-3.0-or-later. Its licence texts sit
  beside it (COPYING.LESSER, COPYING). The MIT terms above do NOT apply to those
  files: they keep their own licence, they are unmodified, and they are kept in
  their own directory so they stay identifiable and replaceable — which is what
  the LGPL asks of a work that links it.

  The crafting-station "zero transfer" technique is adapted from SCIE - Skyrim
  Crafting Inventory Extender by ohfor (MIT). SCIE is not a dependency; the
  approach is reimplemented here.
